Why GPL-2.0-or-later: the player links Onion OS's FFmpeg 2.4.14 shared
libraries, which Onion built with --enable-gpl --enable-nonfree (libx264).
FFmpeg's own code is LGPL-2.1-or-later and GPL-2.0-or-later, so a program
linking that build is distributed under the GPL. GPL-2.0-or-later keeps it
compatible with both GPLv2 and GPLv3 code.

What it links at run time (none of it is shipped with the player; the
device already has every file):

  libavformat.so.56, libavcodec.so.56, libavutil.so.54, libswresample.so.1,
  libswscale.so.3
      FFmpeg 2.4.14, from /mnt/SDCARD/.tmp_update/lib/parasyte (Onion OS).
      LGPL-2.1-or-later / GPL-2.0-or-later. https://ffmpeg.org

  libmi_sys.so, libmi_vdec.so, libmi_divp.so, libmi_gfx.so, libmi_common.so
      SigmaStar MI SDK, from /config/lib (device firmware). Proprietary,
      Sigmastar Technology Corp. Used through their public C API only.

  libpadsp.so
      Onion OS / Miyoo audio shim (/mnt/SDCARD/miyoo/lib or /customer/lib),
      loaded with dlopen() to reach Onion's audioserver.

  glibc (libc, libm, libpthread, libdl) from the device.

Where the build gets its headers (tools/fetch-deps.sh; every download is
checked against a SHA-256):

  FFmpeg 2.4.14 public headers, from the official release tarball
      https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-2.4.14.tar.xz
      sha256 736567ee95115876d7af7f99f2fa565417c351b748bdc05973618980da1df037
      (configure + "make install-headers" only).

  SigmaStar MI SDK headers (mi_common, mi_sys, mi_vdec, mi_divp, mi_gfx and
  their _datatype headers), from steward-fu/sdl2 ("SDL v2.0 Ported for
  Miyoo Mini (Plus)", LGPL-2.1 for the port itself) at commit
  0631abc8e8916db6f9bc7e2afd0c22913d092a29, directory mini/inc. The headers
  carry Sigmastar's copyright notice; they are fetched at build time and
  are not part of this repository.

Linking: the device's own .so files (tools/import-device-libs.sh, checked
by SHA-256) are used as the link sysroot. libavcodec.so.56 is 45 MB and did
not survive the device's Wi-Fi, so tools/build-linkonly-avcodec.sh can
build a link-only copy from the same FFmpeg 2.4.14 tarball instead (same
soname and LIBAVCODEC_56 symbol versions). Either way only the device's
own library is loaded at run time.

